            <title>[LU-21152] FLR: mirror delete with the file itself as the victim fails with -EINVAL</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21152</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lfs mirror split -d&lt;/tt&gt; first tries to destroy the mirror in place: the victim fd is the file itself (&lt;tt&gt;fd == fdv&lt;/tt&gt;, the "purge" path). On master the MDS refuses that with -EINVAL:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;mdd_xattr_split() -&amp;gt; lod_declare_xattr_set() -&amp;gt; lod_save_layout_gen_intrans()
"gen changed from 5 to 6 in trans declaration"
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The check comes from &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17048" title="Crash in lod_declare_update_extents" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17048"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17048&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (2023). The split modifies the layout of the same object twice while the transaction is declared, so the second declare sees a new generation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lfs&lt;/tt&gt; hides this. On -EINVAL or -EBUSY it assumes an old MDS ("could be old MDS which prohibit fd==fdv") and retries with a volatile file in the parent directory. So the in-place path, which needs no parent directory access, never works on a current MDS. A caller without a &lt;tt&gt;lfs&lt;/tt&gt;-style fallback gets -EINVAL.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Found while writing &lt;tt&gt;llapi_mirror_split()&lt;/tt&gt; for lfu-purge (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20462" title="Lustre Find Utility (LFU)" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20462"&gt;LU-20462&lt;/a&gt;), on master with a 2-mirror file.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
